  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Corrected the SageMath 10.9/Sage.js Matrix and Vector audit for the current architecture: dense ZZ and QQ matrices canonically own generated FmpzMatrix and FmpqMatrix resources, GF(7) owns packed residues and exposes 27 typed kernels, and exact packed declarations are compatibility boundaries rather than canonical storage. Updated deterministic storage/resource witnesses, declaration counts, vector mutability coverage, the 18-case performance audit, and the write-disjoint Sage Days lane map.",
    "risks": [
      "Sage dir() counts include broad inherited category methods, so the audit separates name coverage from 69 focused operational witnesses.",
      "Performance limits are coarse cross-platform API regressions; the existing ring-specific dense-matrix gates remain authoritative.",
      "The declaration-count ratchets intentionally require review when generated exact-resource operations are renamed or consolidated."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Start the write-disjoint linear-vector-contract, linear-matrix-selection, and linear-matrix-predicates preparation lanes described in docs/SAGE-DAYS-LINEAR-ALGEBRA-API.md.",
      "Use a short integration-owned lane for each reviewed helper batch that edits src/baselib/matrix.py and updates the audit snapshot.",
      "Refresh the Sage 10.9 name oracle only when the pinned upstream surface or the deliberate Sage.js public API changes."
    ]
